Found while implementing #89 (AKIAnthropic), from public docs only — NOT live verified.

Engine::AKIOpenAI composes Role::HermesTools with the comment:

  # AKI's /openai/v1 endpoint does not support native tool parameters

AKI.IO's current public docs contradict that. https://aki.io/docs/compatibility/for-ai-coding-agents/
section "B. Tool Calling (Function Calling)" states:

  "AKI.IO supports OpenAI-standard tool calling. Pass your tools in the tools array.
   Use tool_choice: auto to let the model decide. When executing a tool, append the tool
   result as a message with role: tool and the matching tool_call_id."

The same page carries a per-model support table (Tool Calling / JSON Mode): gpt-oss-120b,
gemma4-chat-26b, kimi-k2.7-code-1100b, minimax-m2.5-230b, mistral4-119b, qwen3.6-chat-35b
= supported; apertus-chat-70b, llama3-chat-8b, llama3-chat-70b = "Basic Support".

Either the provider gained native tool support since the hermes decision, or the docs
overstate it. Needs ONE live probe with a real AKI key (tools array + tool_choice auto against
/openai/v1/chat/completions) before changing tool_wire_format — the hermes fallback works
either way, so this is not urgent.

If native tools are real, the same question applies to Engine::AKIAnthropic (#89), which
currently inherits the anthropic tool wire format untested (AKI does not document tools on
/anthropic at all).

